// Shared build settings for every target and configuration.
//
// Signing carries no developer identity in the repo. The Team ID lives only in
// Config/Local.xcconfig, which is git-ignored. Signing style is Automatic (set
// in project.yml). A File Provider extension will not load ad-hoc, so running it
// in Finder needs a real team — but `mise run build` passes
// CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO, so a checkout with no Local.xcconfig still compiles.

// Empty by default; Config/Local.xcconfig overrides with a real Team ID (it is
// included last, so its value wins). CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY is deliberately NOT
// pinned: with several "Apple Development" certs across teams, pinning the
// generic name lets the wrong (other-team) cert win and embeds no profile.
// Leaving it to automatic signing picks the cert matching DEVELOPMENT_TEAM.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// Per-contributor Team ID. The `?` makes it optional, so a fresh checkout
// without the file still compiles (unsigned, via CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO).
#include? "Local.xcconfig"

// The App Group the agent and extension share (socket + File Provider document
// group). On macOS an App Group is <TeamID>.<name>, so it is composed from the
// local Team ID here — keeping the team-specific value out of the repo while
// giving both targets and the Info.plist one definition (referenced as
// $(WUSEL_APP_GROUP)).
WUSEL_APP_GROUP = $(DEVELOPMENT_TEAM).at.itbh.wusel
